 Shows the Ethernet interface: its Ethernet address, IP address, mask,
 broadcast address and gateway, the time left on the DHCP lease, the
 name servers, and the packets and bytes received and sent, with
 errors.

 Format:
     IFCONFIG
*Example
     $ IFCONFIG
     XE0: flags=UP,BROADCAST  mtu 1500
          ether 08:00:2b:05:06:07
          inet 192.168.50.53  netmask 255.255.254.0
               broadcast 192.168.51.255
          gateway 192.168.50.1  (DHCP, lease 23:57:56 left)
          RX packets 235  bytes 76672  errors 0
          TX packets 2  bytes 684  errors 0
